<title>USA: FEDERAL EXPRESS TO LIMIT SAT PICKUP SERVICE.</title>
<headline>FEDERAL EXPRESS TO LIMIT SAT PICKUP SERVICE.</headline>
<dateline>MEMPHIS, Tenn. 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Express Corp said Thursday that it will limit its pickup service on Saturday to focus on deliveries so that it can get more packages to their destinations as soon as possible.</p>
<p>The company said the move is related to the strike plaguing rival United Parcel Service of America Inc, which has given way to an increase in business at FedEx.</p>
<p>Deliveries will continue as scheduled, and the service adjustment will affect only pickups, the company said.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
